{
  "title": "Measure the database after photos moved to files; consider hourly snapshots",
  "description": "Photo bytes now live in <DATABASE_URL>-photos/ instead of the SQLite file (server/src/photos/store.rs), and the first startup after that change moves existing BLOBs out, drops the columns and VACUUMs. \
That change couldn't be measured against real data when it landed. \
On a copy of prod (never prod itself): copy the database with `sqlite3 -readonly <db> \"VACUUM INTO '/tmp/copy.sqlite'\"`, note its size, start a server on the copy (or run `ramekin-server backup` against it after a startup), and compare the file size and the photos directory size afterwards. \
Spot-check that photos and thumbnails load from the copy. \
If the database is now small, switch backup.rs's INTERVAL from daily back to hourly (and update doc/sqlite-cutover.md's Backups section and dev.env.example). \
Related: p4-compress-fetched-html, the other large thing in the file.",
